# gnome.hide — desktop-file IDs to hide from the GNOME app grid.
# Consumed by modules/07-gnome-shell.sh, which copies each system .desktop into
# ~/.local/share/applications and sets NoDisplay=true on the copy. A user-level
# file of the same name shadows the system one, so nothing is deleted and
# `apt-get install --reinstall` cannot undo it.
#
# One ID per line, WITHOUT the .desktop suffix. IDs with no system file are
# skipped silently — this list is shared across boxes that install different sets.
#
# Hiding is NOT uninstalling. Every entry below stays fully runnable from a
# terminal; it just stops occupying a tile in a grid you scroll with your eyes.

# --- daemons and libraries that ship a launcher for no reason ---
picom                 # compositor; started by the i3 config, never by hand
feh                   # image viewer used as the i3 wallpaper setter
lstopo                # hwloc topology viewer

# --- duplicates: two entries, one application ---
com.brave.Browser     # duplicate of brave-browser.desktop (the one we pin)
code-url-handler      # protocol handler for code.desktop, not a second VS Code

# --- interpreters and runtimes that are not "apps" ---
python3.14
openjdk-21-java
openjdk-25-java

# --- X11 leftovers that are meaningless in a Wayland GNOME session ---
debian-xterm
debian-uxterm
i3                    # the i3 SESSION is picked at the greeter, not launched here
rofi-theme-selector   # rofi itself is bound to a key in the i3 config
arandr                # GNOME has Settings > Displays
